    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d742">

                <pb facs="0685" n="678" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg678"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/11047: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-12T19:00:00-05:00">November 12, 1937—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>544. Reference Commander-in-Chief’s 0012—1930 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >1826</hi>].<anchor n="14" xml:id="d742-f1"/> With regard to Japanese use of
                    Soochow Creek, Department is of the opinion that action, if any, in opposition
                    thereto should be confined solely to appropriate representations. Inform
                    Commander-in-Chief.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
